<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Three screens of the settings app:

  * Dictionary, the list of words the keyboard learned from your typing.
  * Never suggest, the list of words the keyboard keeps out of suggestions.
  * Backup, which writes one file with your keyboard in it and reads it back.

  The backup screen names the parts of that file (settings, themes, clipboard
  and so on) in three places: the toggles that select what goes in, the dialog
  that lists what a file holds, and the message after a restore. The message
  puts the name in the middle of a sentence, so each name has a second value in
  lower case. A translation cannot make a lower-case form on its own.
-->
